        "original_id": "efce6b1c-4dde-59b1-bad8-9373f58569fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"She's a Woman\", \"I Feel Fine\"\n- People: Paul McCartney, John Lennon\n- Companies: the Beatles\n- Concepts: Lennon–McCartney, guitar feedback\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, the Beatles released \"I Feel Fine\" as the A-side of their eighth British single.\n- In 1964, the Beatles released \"She's a Woman\" as the B-side to \"I Feel Fine\", their last single release of that year.\n- \"I Feel Fine\" was written by John Lennon and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- \"She's a Woman\" was written mainly by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- \"I Feel Fine\" has one of the first uses of guitar feedback in popular music.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f95c9ad3-c1b8-544a-8e30-1eb2bb03d6e5",
        "text": "Page: She's a Woman. Sentence: \"She's a Woman\" is a song by the Beatles, written mainly by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\nPage: She's a Woman. Sentence: It was released as the B-side to \"I Feel Fine\" in 1964, their last single release that year.\nPage: I Feel Fine. Sentence: \"I Feel Fine\" is a song written by John Lennon (credited to Lennon–McCartney) and released in 1964 by the Beatles as the A-side of their eighth British single.\nPage: I Feel Fine. Sentence: The song has one of the first uses of guitar feedback in popular music.",
